    "plotType": "Cyclogram (one joint angle vs. another, closed loop)",
    "description": "An angle–angle diagram (cyclogram) plots one joint's angle against another joint's angle over the gait cycle — classically knee flexion against hip flexion — producing a closed loop rather than two separate time curves. The shape of the loop captures the coordination between the two joints: how they flex and extend relative to each other moment by moment. It is prized in gait analysis because inter-joint coordination is hard to see in side-by-side time plots but jumps out as a distinctive loop shape here.",
